  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Dell Federal Systems L P obligated $2.3B in FY2026 to date on federal contracts. Dell Federal Systems L P won 651 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $3.6M, and obligations are up 75.3% year over year. Dell Federal Systems L P received the largest share of FY2026 obligations from the Department of Defense, which obligated $1.1B. Dell Federal Systems L P also sold to civilian agencies: the Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $553M, the Department of Homeland Security obligated $300M, and the Department of Health and Human Services obligated $140M. Dell Federal Systems L P’s NAICS breakdown for FY2026 to date shows Software Publishers as the top market with $2B, followed by additional Software Publishers entries at $126M and Electronic Computer Manufacturing at $120M. Historical obligations show that Dell Federal Systems L P’s obligations were $1.6B in FY21, $1.7B in FY22, $1.4B in FY23, $1.5B in FY24, and $1.3B in FY25. Current-year totals are fiscal year to date and therefore partial.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies are buying from Dell Federal Systems L P?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $1.1B in FY2026 to date. The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $553M and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $300M. Other notable buyers include the Department of Health and Human Services at $140M and the Department of Commerce at $62.4M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What product and service markets is Dell Federal Systems L P serving?",
        "body": "Software Publishers is the dominant market with $2B in FY2026 to date and an additional Software Publishers entry at $126M. Dell Federal Systems L P also has obligations in Electronic Computer Manufacturing at $120M and Other Computer Related Services at $70.1M. Smaller markets include Computer Storage Device Manufacturing at $4.6M and Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $12.8M."
      }
    ]
  },
